.TH EXPRESSO 1 "2026-09-29" "expresso" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
expresso \- keep the system awake for a while, or indefinitely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B expresso
.I command
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B expresso
temporarily prevents the system from sleeping, using
.BR systemd-inhibit (1)
and transient
.BR systemd-run (1)
user units. It can be driven from the command line or through a
.BR rofi (1)
menu.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI start " time"
Start keeping the system awake. A bare number is taken as minutes.
Accepted forms include
.BR 15 ,
.BR 15m ,
.BR 90s ,
.BR 2h ,
and
.B inf
or
.B infinite
for no time limit. Starting again replaces the current lock.
.TP
.B stop
Cancel the active lock.
.TP
.B status
Print the time remaining,
.BR Infinite ,
or
.BR Inactive .
.TP
.B menu
Open the interactive rofi menu.
.TP
.BR version ", " \-\-version ", " \-V
Print the version.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-\-help ", " \-h
Print usage information.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Settings are read from
.IR $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/expresso/expresso.conf
(default
.IR ~/.config/expresso/expresso.conf ).
.TP
.B BLOCK_LID="true"
Also inhibit the laptop lid switch.
.TP
.B BLOCK_IDLE="true"
Also prevent Wayland idle daemons from dimming or locking the screen.
Requires
.BR wayland-idle-inhibitor.py .
.PP
An example is installed at
.IR /usr/share/doc/expresso/expresso.conf.example .
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
expresso start 30
expresso start 2h
expresso start inf
expresso status
expresso stop
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR systemd-run (1),
.BR rofi (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/Davi-S/expresso/issues
